I love the ability to return structured error types with a `statusCode` so that we don't need to call `.setStatus` and make everything a `500`, even if it's not.

I do think that we could make this more reusable, although this is a nit really and i dont think it's worth perfecting unless you fire off claude and it one shots it.

here's how i would do it, and we could adopt this incrementally into the codebase

```
export interface BackendError {
  // a human readable message for the user
  message: string;
  // optional, detailed error message for debugging
  details?: string;
  // the http status code to return to the user
  statusCode: number;
}
```

